      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fyi making this non-final is fairly expensive according to tim, because it means it can\u0027t be inlined and a method call is really expensive on little cores due to lacking branch prediction.\n\nI wonder if this could be arranged to avoid this...  either putting more of the logic for this stuff in the base class, or maybe having two maps, one for primitive types, the other for serializable/parcelable objects?",
