    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "820d87ad_e4e52989",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/BaseBundle.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 461,
      "author": {
        "id": 1133744
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-10T17:44:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are only a few usages which seem fine indeed. What did you have in mind to optimize this?\n\nI\u0027m thinking we go over the map comparing and when we see a lazy value we do:\n* If the other is a live object we deserialize the lazy and compare the resulting objects.\n* If both are lazy, we can compare the payload, but I have a few questions here:\n\n1) If we use compareData(), does that handle Binder \u0026 FDs properly? If not, is there a method we could use?\n\n2) We need to compare a subsection of parcel (position + length parameters), not the entire parcel. In that case, I don\u0027t see a method for comparison (please correct me if I\u0027m wrong), is it worth copying over the parcel and comparing the copies rather than deserializing and comparing the result?",
      "parentUuid": "a243bf6e_c4e71360",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 459,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 461,
        "endChar": 0
      },
