      "writtenOn": "2021-08-12T22:53:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess we should improve my javadoc for this to make it more clear what it does. :)  One concern I have is that with this change, people will no longer need to wrry about many of the situations now where they access a Bundle (such as the rule to never touch a user-supplied Bundle in the system process).  But if you are now thinking that way, this function is something you need to stay away from because by unparcelling everything you end up with the same old problems.\n\nThat said...  note that one of the cases where we can already (incorrectly) decide that the two are not equal is if one is parceled and the other isn\u0027t.  So I think it would be semantically consistent to say that if a particular entry in the map is parceled and the other isn\u0027t, that is also not equal.  (And likewise if they are both parceled, we already do a raw comparison of the parceled data.)\n\nOf course that *will* be a change from the current semantics, if you have received a Bundle, and do kindofEquals() after you tried to retrieve a value from it (and caused it to be unparceled).  I wonder if that is an issue, I think one of the main reasons for this method is for the system process to be able to do comparisons of bundles without unparceling things from apps?",
      "parentUuid": "3458ca4a_5197519c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 459,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 461,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "600328e150292275cce234d23f3dd57163e08ca3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07756e7e_a59a7c45",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/BaseBundle.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
