      "writtenOn": "2021-08-10T17:44:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the concern about the overhead of the \u0027if\u0027 check? (Because primitives will not enter that \u0027if\u0027 branch..)\n\nIn that case, I can bypass this call and do mMap.get(\u003ckey\u003e) directly for primitive types in their getters. Because if we handle the CCE in custom types we\u0027d put custom code in those anyway (and it seems like the performance concern is with primitives, not those), would that work for you?",
      "parentUuid": "d0655b06_f1f903ad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1282,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1289,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "600328e150292275cce234d23f3dd57163e08ca3",
