    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ceb6945_7ea70e48",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Bundle.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1289,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059882
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-12T22:53:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah I think for primitives we should just directly pull from the map.  Actually that seems pretty great -- we know it can only be the primitive object type, and anything else is going to be a type failure, and then we can actually avoid unparceling the data in the failure case which just doing that can be problematic (for example a security exploit trying to get the system to unparcel some type that will cause problems).  To help with debugging, we could peek in the parcel data to see the class type it would be and report that.",
      "parentUuid": "96ab9962_7bb0a3ec",
